+# v32 — client-area input, confirmed camera selection and game-day sightings
+
+- Native Windows input now asks for the real client area and hit-tests pointer
+  positions. Resize borders and title bars never receive map clicks or drags.
+  A held gesture temporarily confines the cursor to the client area and restores
+  the previous confinement after release, cancellation or failure. GetCursorPos
+  verifies the actual destination; redirected input stops before a click.
+- The four exact map control boxes remain unchanged. Native window chrome is
+  excluded using Windows geometry; no arbitrary map padding is added.
+- Held motion uses smaller, paced cursor steps and measured optical flow on map
+  terrain. Forward/backward and texture checks validate flow; ambiguous frames
+  use the existing SIFT path. Release still happens after a stationary pause.
+- A map tap is no longer treated as successful merely because it was sent.
+  Delayed automatic closure is allowed; otherwise the white camera outline must
+  match the selected point before Back. A click ripple is not confirmation.
+  One ignored tap is retried against fresh alignment. Failed selection stays
+  unchecked and cannot create a false empty visit or advance the Spy history.
+- Gem Sniper always clicks a confirmed gem's centre once and stops. Broad right
+  edge/HUD-region click vetoes are removed. A one-frame score drop does not
+  cancel an already confirmed find. A fresh image can refine its position;
+  native focus, resize, obstruction, finite-image bounds and F10 checks remain.
+  Gem Spy remains observation-only.
+- The top-right Sniper counter shows seen gems / 5. Photo completion/replayed
+  events do not double count. Finds during the photo cooldown still count.
+  The counter persists across app restarts, route changes and Reset checks.
+- The counter and standard history Today only use the same game day: 16:00
+  Europe/Sofia through just before the next 16:00. Midnight does not reset it.
+  Daylight-saving transitions are included; tzdata is pinned and bundled into
+  the Windows EXE. Show all and original history rows remain available.
+
+The Windows build checks native mouse delivery, client-border rejection,
+confinement restoration and F10 on its own test window; UI checks cover the
+counter, original source history, saved routes and Spy integration. The full
+route uses real atlas pixels and simulated input. These are not live BlueStacks
+or game-account tests. The user's recording informed the border/click fixes;
+private video frames are not distributed in the release.
